2           USING THE INVALUE STATEMENT
                                                           The SAS System

3               This program creates an informat to read in or convert data with an INPUT statement or function.
4               Keywords: PROC FORMAT, INFORMAT, INVALUE
5               SAS Versions: SAS 9, SAS Viya
6               Documentation:
6        ! https://documentation.sas.com/?cdcId=pgmsascdc&cdcVersion=default&docsetId=proc&docsetTarget=p1xidhqypi0fnwn1if8opjpqpbmn
6        ! .htm
7               1. The INVALUE statement creates an informat that can be used to read data.
8               2. In the DATA step, the second field is first as a string and assigned to the column String.
9                  The second field is read again using the EVAL informat and assigned to the column Evaluation.
10              3. View the results of using the informat in PROC PRINT and PROC MEANS.
11         ************************************************************************************************/
12         
13         proc format;
13       !                                                     /*1*/
14            invalue eval
15               'Excellent'=4
16                    'Good'=3
17                    'Fair'=2
18                    'Poor'=1
19            ;
NOTE: Informat EVAL has been output.
20         run;

